[Music]  welcome to max tech  and this is our review of the iphone 12  [Music]  pro  on the surface the iphone 12 pro seems  like it's basically the same phone from  last year  just with an updated design and a couple  of added features  but in reality it's actually the biggest  generational leap since the iphone 6s  which was such a solid phone that apple  struggled for years  trying to get people to upgrade to a  newer iphone  so in this review i'm going to explain  why the iphone 12  pro is so good that it's following in  the 6s footsteps  hello and welcome back going back to  apple's iphone event  a lot of people were quite disappointed  with the iphone 12 lineup  saying that nothing has really changed  but that's far from the truth  just like the iphone 11 pro from last  year the iphone 12  pro ended up being so much better than i  expected  when i finally got my hands on it and  started testing it out  in fact there are so many improvements  that apple didn't mention  during the event so in this review  instead of just giving you guys  all the specs you've already heard in  other reviews like the new 814 bionic  chip  the lidar scanner the six gigs of ram  and  everything else i'm gonna talk about the  things that actually  matter in everyday life and i'm also  gonna talk about the most controversial  topics  like the real reason why apple got rid  of the power adapter and the wired  earbuds  that used to come inside of the box and  also the whole thing about 5g  and battery life which a lot of people  are misunderstanding  and throwing under the bus so let's get  right into it this year  things are a bit different because i  can't order the 12  pro max that i want until next month  but i did buy my wife the 6.1 inch 12  pro which she's been using for the past  week  so for this review i asked her if she  noticed anything different coming from  her iphone 11 pro  and i was shocked by the amount of  improvements that she noticed  but before we get into that i want to  talk about why i think the iphone 12  pro is so great that it's easily worth  upgrading from an older iphone  maybe even the iphone 11 pro i  personally believe that there are  three reasons why people should upgrade  to a new phone  and the iphone 12 pro completely nails  all three of them the first one is that  the phone has to feel  different because when you're spending  this much money  you don't want it to feel like your  previous phone that exact reason  is why so little people upgraded from  the iphone 10  to the iphone 10s they were so similar  that you couldn't even tell them apart  but when i first got the iphone 12 pro  in my hands  i was completely blown away because it  feels like a totally  different phone and i'm reminded of that  every time i pick it up  yes that's due to the new flat sides  which apple  executed perfectly the edges are  barely rounded into the flat sides but  at the same time  both the glass on the front and the  glass on the back  are perfectly flush with the stainless  steel band  seriously if you haven't held the iphone  12 in your hands  you have to go find one because it feels  so much  better than you'd expect my wife was  initially stunned by the new design  but after a couple of days she fell in  love  with their iphone 12 pro saying that  it's so much  easier to hold and she absolutely loves  how clean and smooth  the new design looks being flat all the  way around  and because the front glass is also now  completely flat apple was able to make  the bezels  quite a bit more thin and thanks to  bumping up the display to 6.1 inches  my wife told me that she loves how much  more immersive  the display in the phone feels and on  top of that apple has improved the  speakers  being louder and sounding better than  the ones on the iphone 11 pro  which were already a massive improvement  compared to older iphones  so this really helps it feel like you  have a totally different phone  now the second reason why people should  upgrade to a new phone is  reliability yes we've got the new a14  bionic chip which is  the fastest iphone chip ever obviously  but honestly it doesn't really make the  iphone  feel any faster than before and like i  say  every single year the performance  differences actually go  directly towards efficiency and camera  improvements  which i'll get into in just a minute one  major thing i complained about last year  was that the 11 pro still only had  four gigabytes of ram and that led to  apps closing in the background  which was extremely annoying but now the  iphone 12 pro  finally has 6 gigs of ram and so far i  haven't experienced any issues yet  we also now have the ceramic shield  front glass  which is supposed to have much better  drop protection  and since i use my iphones naked without  a case  this gives me a lot of extra peace of  mind and now  let's get into all of that 5g and  battery life controversy  yes the battery is quite a bit smaller  than it was  last year and that's because apple had  to make the iphone quite a bit thinner  so the squared off edges don't make it  feel too thick  and because of the smaller battery the  12 pro now gets about one hour less of  battery life  compared to the iphone 11 pro according  to mr who's the boss  and i think it's because of the a14's  killer graphics performance  which demands more power in the antutu  graphics test  that he was running but considering the  fact that the display is now  larger 6.1 inches compared to the  previous 5.8  it's actually not too bad of a hit and  that brings us to the controversy of  5g which can lead to even worse battery  life  but there are two very good solutions  that people  aren't talking about or at least they're  misunderstanding  apple created the smart data mode which  only turns on 5g  when you actually need it which means  that you could potentially  go through a full day without 5g being  turned on  even once which means that it doesn't  impact battery life at  all now i know what you're gonna say  what's the point of upgrading if it's  not even using  5g well this might surprise you  but the even bigger deal is the fact  that apple  is finally using qualcomm's snapdragon  x55 modem in the new iphone 12 lineup  and this new modem  is the real game changer so here are a  couple of screenshots i took  using my iphone 11 pro and the new 12  pro in my basement  and as you can see the reception is  terrible  on my 11 pro and simply switching to the  12 pro using  lte i got 25 times faster download  speeds  and 5g was actually slower because it  doesn't seem to penetrate into basements  that well  i then went upstairs and now 5g is  actually giving us a huge advantage  as high as 87 megabits per second  using t-mobile's low band 5g which is  basically  everywhere in my city and not the  millimeter wave 5g  which i think shouldn't even matter  because you can move a couple of feet  and lose millimeter wave and now while  upstairs in my house the lte on the 12  pro isn't much faster than the 11 pro  for download speeds the upload speeds  improved quite a bit as well  so here's the thing about 5g and the new  iphones  if you're worried about battery life  just turn  off 5g and enjoy very reliable lte  speeds that are now much faster as you  guys saw in my basement  not only that but after only a week my  wife has already noticed much better  cellular service  all over town including a friend's house  where she always struggled with bad  service on her previous iphone 11 pro  but now this qualcomm modem is a game  changer  without even considering 5g so i ended  up simply  turning off 5g on my wife's iphone 12  pro  because she honestly doesn't like 5g and  she would much  rather have better battery life instead  now let's finally get into the third  reason why i think  people should upgrade to a new phone and  that's the feature set  i think one of the biggest deals for the  iphone 12 lineup is  the new mac save feature apple basically  created  a new ecosystem of accessories that can  more conveniently attach to the iphone  using magnets like of course the mac  safe wallet  that i'm still patiently waiting for  there are also now pop sockets that are  coming to the iphone 12  no longer requiring a sticky adhesive to  hold on  car mounts are about to become so much  more convenient  with magnets built into the iphone  itself and there are so many  possibilities that we haven't realized  yet  since this is the first week since the  iphone 12 has been released  and i honestly believe that after a full  year the market is gonna be flooded  with magsafe accessories and this  feature itself  is gonna get people to upgrade now  beyond that  the absolute number one feature that i  didn't expect to get  improved this much is the camera  performance  that was the one thing that my wife  wouldn't stop talking about  she was so impressed by how every photo  looked more  sharp on the iphone 12 pro especially  the ultra wide camera which looks so  much better than before  and this is odd because it's literally  the same exact camera sensor and lens  from the 11 pros ultrawide camera the  big difference  is in the new software improvements we  now have smart hdr3  which uses ai to optimize various parts  of the scene  we also now have night mode on every  single camera  which is a game changer because you'd be  limited to the wide lens on the 11 pro  if you wanted great looking nighttime  shots  and now selfies look amazing in the dark  even pitch black as you can see right  here  and on top of that the iphone 12 pro  comes with a new  lidar scanner which is basically like an  upscaled version of face id  that helps with 3d depth mapping and  tracking  the lidar scanner enables nighttime  portrait photos  which we've never had before because  portrait shots require much more light  and as you can tell these photos turn  out great  but what you might not know is that the  iphone 12 pro actually uses the lidar  scanner  for video recording in the dark as well  check out the difference between these  three generations of  iphones the iphone 10s doesn't even try  to focus  while the 11 pro hunts for focus  non-stop  but the 12 pro gets it spot on every  time  thanks to using the lidar scanner but  the absolute  biggest deal of all is getting deep  fusion on  every single camera including the selfie  camera  it basically takes multiple photos in  the blink of an eye  and then combines the data from multiple  photos  into one compressing the detail  into a tightly packed and incredibly  sharp photo  that's why everything from ultrawide  photos to zoom  shots and even selfies look so much more  detailed than before  even though the actual megapixels of the  sensors  haven't changed and i need to remind you  that all of these major software  improvements  are possible because of the massive  performance improvement  of the a14 bionic chip since all of this  happens in real time  unlike other phones like the pixel 5  which makes you wait for seconds  to finish processing before you can see  things like the background blur and the  true dynamic range  apple wants this type of processing to  happen right away  and the a14 chip allows them to enable  processor heavy features  like deep fusion and smart hdr3 on all  of the lenses  so with all of that said the iphone 12  pro  absolutely nails the three things that i  believe  matter the most in terms of iphone  upgradability  and with that i want to finish with the  real reason why  apple didn't include a charger or wired  earbuds in the box  yes i guess in a way it does help the  environment  but it honestly helps apple much more  because they ditched the charger  and the earbuds they not only save money  on those two items  but they're now able to make every  iphone box  twice as small as before saving them  massive amounts of cash  in terms of material transportation  inventory and shipping costs not only  that but it forces people to buy  wireless air pods and a fast charger  which means  even more potential profit for apple now  while that makes them seem very  evil and greedy let me remind you  that apple kept the price of the iphone  12 pro  at the exact same 999 dollars  while adding a bunch of expensive  features  the top of the line 5g modem from  qualcomm definitely wasn't cheap  we now have 6 gigs of ram instead of 4  128 gigs of base storage instead of 64  a brand new flat edge design which  requires retooling  better water resistance a brand new 5  nanometer chip from tsmc  a brand new wide sensor from sony  new ceramic shield glass from corning a  new lidar scanner for the first time  ever  on any iphone and of course the new  magsafe  built right into the iphone we're  basically getting a lot of extra  features and hardware this year  at the exact same price while a lot of  other android phones  are getting more expensive thanks to 5g  support  or in the case of the pixel 5 which  sacrifices flagship specs  and features to save money instead apple  is giving us  brand new tech and top of the line  hardware for the same price as before  and they're sacrificing the charger and  earbuds to do it  which is actually okay with me because i  already have a fast charger  and i already have earpods like many  other people out there  so with all of that said let me wrap up  this review with the three  biggest reasons why anyone should  upgrade to the iphone 12 pro  fast and reliable lte cellular service  major camera improvements thanks to the  a14 bionic chip  and finally the new flat redesign which  makes it feel like you have  a totally different phone and that truly  matters for  upgradability so if you choose to  upgrade to an iphone 12  or 12 pro it's gonna feel modern for the  next few years  since the rounded side redesign of the  iphone 6  lasted for five generations before this  flat side design change so to be  completely honest  there has never been a better time to  upgrade to a new iphone  hopefully you guys enjoyed this review  and if you did go ahead and click the  circle above to subscribe  because i'm gonna be reviewing the  iphone 12 pro max  as soon as i get my hands on it next  month and also be sure to check out our  camera comparisons  right over there thanks for watching and  we'll see you  in the next one  you

